From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerry Zhao <jerryz123@berkeley.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] Do not require optional software-check delegation in Sm
Purpose: Keeps the base Sm CSR walk independent of CFI-specific exception causes.
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

The software-check exception at cause 18 belongs to Zicfilp/Zicfiss. An Sm
implementation without either extension may leave medeleg[18] read-only zero.
The generic CSR walk must not require that bit to retain a write.

diff --git a/generators/testgen/src/testgen/priv/extensions/Sm.py b/generators/testgen/src/testgen/priv/extensions/Sm.py
--- a/generators/testgen/src/testgen/priv/extensions/Sm.py
+++ b/generators/testgen/src/testgen/priv/extensions/Sm.py
@@ -608,7 +608,7 @@ def _generate_mcsr_tests(test_data: TestData, test_chunks: list) -> None:
     csrm = [
         (
             "medeleg",
-            0xDBBFE,
-        ),  # mask off custom bits and reserved bits; instr misaligned [0] depends on ZCA_SUPPORTED so don't check it
+            0x9BBFE,
+        ),  # omit optional software-check [18]; instr misaligned [0] depends on ZCA_SUPPORTED
         ("mideleg", 0xFFFF),  # limit to standard interrupt bits
         ("mie", 0xFFFF),  # limit to standard interrupt bits
